Z||000000||94ZonCrack||03-26-2001||12:17 PM||||Holy Crap what a pain. I pulled the engine from an 87 eldorado. I know it's kinda weak on power. Does anyone know of anyone that has performance upgrades for these engines? Aftermarket cams, heads, intake?<P>I guess next weekend I'll be pulling out the iron duke. Is there a way to tell if the engine is any good with it out of the car. It doesnt leak oil. I don't know anything else about it though.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||ray b||03-26-2001||12:46 PM||||test compression or leekdown test [see how long air pressure takes to leeks out].<BR>4.1 has no power and bad head gaskets try to find a 4.9 and then hop it up. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||03-26-2001||03:46 PM||||if i were you replace the plugs and whatever gaskets you can  before you put it in the car, there are no aftermarket parts that i know of for this engine, if you find a place let me know, you could upgrade the ignition though<P><BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bluemagic||03-26-2001||04:18 PM||||I am doing a 4.9 cadillac conversion,yes it is true the 4.1 is low on horsepower (145)hp and there is not any after market parts available but with a good exhaust system,a msd and high output coil you should be satisfied for the money spent. ||||reg||3
Z||000004||rockcrawl||03-26-2001||05:45 PM||||Was that 4.1 mounted transversly in the Eldorado? I know the Eldorado 4.1 was longitudinal up until '85 and they had a different bolt pattern on the bellhousing.||||reg||1
